", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Per release history, v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production (v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging and v2.3.1 unhealthy in production). Action taken: rolled back checkout-api to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry completed the rollback; all three regions now run v2.3.0, status healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager review.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024-incident"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created so I don't open a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011xJfn2d4ruXDtm41m3V68R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and the service is healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release running before the rollback.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident is INC-0001, open and describing the rollback, the partial failure, and the retry. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. It showed the incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: investigate why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager review.", "type": "text"}]}]}